---
export const prerender = true;

import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/sheet.css';
import { canonicalTags, newestFirst } from '../utils/content';

const posts = newestFirst(await getCollection('posts'));
const tagCount = canonicalTags(posts).length;
---

<Base title="About" description="Why Rabbit Holes is kept as a public commonplace book." active="about">
  <main class="sheet">
    <div class="kicker">About · who keeps this, and why</div>
    <h1>Hi, I’m Bhuvan.</h1>
    <p class="strap">Searching for new rabbit holes.</p>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">Rabbit holes</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="rubric">Hi, I’m Bhuvan and I like tumbling down weird and wonderful rabbit holes. I like knowing random things and I think there’s a certain joy in being a dilettante.</p>
        <p>It’s not just me—everyone likes discovering new things, but for whatever reason, most people lose that ability to experience awe and wonder. It’s tempting to blame social media apps and smartphones for this pathology, but that’s too simplistic—they’re not the only reason people seem to have become incurious and, perhaps more tragically, okay with being so.</p>
        <p>This blog is an attempt for me to continue slipping into weird rabbit holes and share them. The hope here is that whatever I share might trip fellow travelers on the internet and send them sliding down a rabbit hole.</p>
        <p>The goal isn’t to be an expert on everything, but to maintain a sense of wonder about the world. Sometimes the most interesting insights come from wandering without a destination in mind.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">All knowledge</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <blockquote class="about-quote">
          <p>Lastly, I confess that I have as vast contemplative ends, as I have moderate civil ends: for I have taken all knowledge to be my province.</p>
          <cite><a href="https://paperlanterns.ink/letter/bacon-burghley-1592/">Francis Bacon</a></cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">Philosophy</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <blockquote class="about-quote">
          <p>The important thing is not to stop questioning. Curiosity has its own reason for existence.</p>
          <cite>Albert Einstein</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="two-inks">
      <div class="section-label">The two inks</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p>Black belongs to the world: a source, a quotation, another person’s title. Red belongs to the collector: why I kept something, where I filed it, and the paths I offer deeper into the garden.</p>
        <ul class="ink-key">
          <li><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--ink)"></span><strong>Black</strong><span>the world and its sources</span></li>
          <li><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--red)"></span><strong>Red</strong><span>the collector’s hand</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">What is here</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p><strong>{posts.length}</strong> published folios across five forms, with <strong>{tagCount}</strong> normalized tags and a smaller set of subjects chosen by hand.</p>
        <p>The numbering never resets. The oldest published leaf is folio one; every new leaf takes the next number.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">How it is made</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p>Built with Astro, served from Cloudflare, and written in Markdown. Bodoni Moda is the display hand, Newsreader is the reading face, and Spline Sans Mono labels the machinery.</p>
        <p>No newsletter modal, no cookie maze. RSS remains the quietest way to follow along.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">Write to me</div>
      <div class="copy">
        <ul class="contact-list">
          <li><a href="mailto:bhuvan@bebhuvan.com"><span>Email</span><span>bhuvan@bebhuvan.com</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="https://twitter.com/bebhuvan"><span>Twitter</span><span>@bebhuvan</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="https://smallweb.blog"><span>Small Web</span><span>smallweb.blog</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/rss.xml"><span>RSS</span><span>follow quietly</span></a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
